        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do rice mills, jute units and potato cold storages need electropolished pipe?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Generally no. Rice milling, parboiling and jute processing are dry or steam-boiler processes, and cold storage uses refrigeration. Electropolished pipe pays off on wet food lines such as potato washing and frying, edible-oil and dairy lines, and clean utilities, where a smooth surface is easier to clean. Tell us your process and we'll say honestly whether it fits."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is 304L enough for a potato washing or frying line, or should I choose 316L?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "304L is the standard grade for food lines and handles normal caustic and acid CIP cycles. Choose 316L if brine or your sanitisers carry chlorides, or the product is acidic. Send us your product and CIP chemistry and we'll confirm the grade. Our internal Ra of 0.4 µm or better sits inside the usual food band of 0.8 µm."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is it worth ordering from Mumbai when Bardhaman has local dealers, and can you combine our order with Durgapur or Kolkata?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For a few plain lengths, a local dealer is usually cheaper at this distance, and we'll say so. We're the better choice when you need a measured Ra, heat-number traceability, a particular size or finish, or the full document pack. If you have several sizes or several sites, send them together and we'll quote one consolidated dispatch with Durgapur, Asansol, Dankuni or Kolkata sites."
